#: 23fdae31b50b428ab164acba3d1738b8
msgid "Values sent to the ESC are checksum-protected"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dshot-escs.rst:12
#: 57ef49cbe734413f9f724c5535a405f5
msgid "Clock differences between the ESC and autopilot don't affect flight performance"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dshot-escs.rst:13
#: d6361ca1c23342e9b1570ab9181bb80e
msgid "ESC calibration is not required"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dshot-escs.rst:15
#: 6263af0b136349008270e7296d372580
msgid "DShot is the underlying ESC control protocol used by :ref:`BLHeli/AM32 <common-blheli32-passthru>` ESCs.  Many BLHeli/AM32 ESC versions offer even more features such as ESC configuration, :ref:`ESC telemetry <blheli32-esc-telemetry>`, LED control and/or :ref:`Bi-directional dshot <bidir-dshot>`.  If choosing a DShot enabled ESC we recommend using one that also supports BLHeli32, AM32, or BLHeli_S."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dshot-escs.rst:18
#: 12f87cd0fa614e07b9b3aaf670f1a4a0
msgid "Only try DShot on ESCs that are known to support it or you will get unpredictable results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dshot-escs.rst:21
#: 9d97eac5d6b048be94a65fc2ed999e5e
msgid "Recently there is a growing number of proprietary and non-proprietary 16 / 32 bit ESCs with firmware that support DShot and other digital ESC protocols, but not BLHeli32/AM32 specific features like passthrough and telemetry. See your ESC's manual for further detail on supported features."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dshot-escs.rst:23
#: 8a9781468c2c4ddeb2132d2bcd01ba37
msgid "most DShot ESCs normally will also operate as normal :ref:`PWM ESCs <common-brushless-escs>`."
msgstr ""

