#: ../../source/docs/common-dshot-escs.rst:121
#: 7744ac275a90426ab9818eccdbb74fa5
msgid "Reversible DShot (aka 3D mode) allows the motor to be spun in either direction which is important for Rover, Boats and :ref:`Planes with reverse thrust <plane:reverse-thrust-setup>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dshot-escs.rst:123
#: d042c5135515449e9b0c34b5bd22a218
msgid "Currently, only BLHeli32, AM32, and BLHeli_S capable reversible DShot ESCs are supported. In order to use one, the output which drives it must be designated with the appropriate bit in the :ref:`SERVO_BLH_3DMASK<SERVO_BLH_3DMASK>` bitmask parameter. This will map the outputs 1000-1500-2000 values to the correct digital values for the ESC to provide FullReverse-Idle-FullForward range operation, respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dshot-escs.rst:125
#: fb7b74e0cc8442d79bd32db483d9efd5
msgid "If :ref:`DShot commands <dshot-commands>` have been enabled then ArduPilot will automatically configure the ESCs to reversible mode (3D mode) at startup, according to the :ref:`SERVO_BLH_3DMASK<SERVO_BLH_3DMASK>`. Enabling :ref:`DShot commands <dshot-commands>` will allow the other DShot commands to be sent to any other ESC configured as DShot by the DShot mask parameters discussed in :ref:`DShot setup instructions <common-dshot-escs>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dshot-escs.rst:127
